From 818673ef868c3e90ddcd8b94dd6dadc2e6a09718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:27:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Batch: regularization of Faltus et al. by kernels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The regularization of Faltus et al. (`Faltus2026` behaviour integrators,
3D and plane strain) adds to the inner forces of an element
`Σ_q w_q det J_q D_qᵀ α (F_q - F0)` and to its stiffness matrix
`α Σ_q w_q det J_q D_qᵀ D_q`, `F0` being the deformation gradient at the
center of the element and `D_q = B_q - B0`. It is now computed by kernels
(new module `MFEMMGIS/Batch/Faltus.hxx`):

- `F0` is computed with the gradients by kernels, from the derivatives of
  the unknowns at the center of the elements (rule of order 0, given by
  `getAdditionalIntegrationRulesForKernels` as for the FBar formulation;
  computation shared with the FBar formulation in
  `computeDeformationGradientAtCenter`), kept by `update` and restored by
  `revert`, and invalid if the gradients are computed element by element;
- the stiffness matrices do not depend on the unknowns and are computed on
  the fly: for a deformation gradient, the block of the nodes `a` and `b`
  of `D_qᵀ D_q` is `d_a · d_b` times the identity, `d` being the
  difference of the derivatives of the shape functions at the point and at
  the center. One thread per pair of nodes for the matrices of the
  elements, per node for the assembled matrix and the diagonal, per element
  for the action.

The inner forces of a behaviour integrator depending on the current
estimate of the solution can only be computed by kernels from gradients
computed by kernels: refused at setup
(`MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator::checkInnerForcesKernelsSupport`). The
regularization is refused in plane stress, where the axial component of
the deformation gradient is not given by the unknowns.
